  "verbalization": "Doxorubicin is implicated in the targeting of MDA-MB-361 through multiple indirect pathways, all of which involve the compound 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid. This compound is identified as a target of both COLO-792 and NCI-H46, which in turn are targets of doxorubicin. The presence of a common target, 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, suggests a potential mechanism of action where doxorubicin influences the activity of this compound, which then affects MDA-MB-361. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible dependency on the metabolic or signaling pathways that are modulated by 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which may be a key mediator in the interaction between doxorubicin and MDA-MB-361. The evidence supports a mechanism where doxorubicin indirectly targets MDA-MB-361 through the activation or modulation of 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which is a shared target across multiple cell lines.",
